    "ddinterOriginalText": "Coadministration of cabozantinib with multidrug resistance-associated proteins (MRP2) inhibitors may increase exposure and toxicity of cabozantinib. In vitro studies have shown MRP2 inhibitors may increase the plasma concentrations of cabozantinib, a MRP2 substrate.",
    "ddinterOriginalManagement": "Caution is advised if cabozantinib is used concomitantly with a MRP2 inhibitor. Monitor for cabozantinib toxicity, such as gastrointestinal perforations and fistulas, hemorrhage, thrombotic events, hypertension, diarrhea, and palmar-plantar erythrodysesthesia. Dose reductions, interruption or discontinuation of cabozantinib may be necessary if toxicity occurs."
