    "ddinterOriginalText": "Coadministration with apalutamide may decrease the plasma concentrations and therapeutic effects of drugs that are substrates of CYP450 3A4, 2C9, 2C19, breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP), uridine diphosphate glucuronosyltransferase (UGT), organic anion transporting polypeptide 1B1 (OATP1B1), and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) efflux transporter. The proposed mechanism involves accelerated clearance via these routes due to apalutamide-mediated induction. The resulting plasma concentrations will depend on the sensitivity of the affected drugs to these isoenzymes.",
